  "response_text": "To run a thread, the chip needs to be \u201ctricked\u201d into thinking it had already been running the thread. This requires setting up the thread\u2019s stack and context, which are the values that would have been in the registers had the thread been already running. This is what it means to \u201cset up a thread\u2019s stack,\u201d \u2013 to add values to the stack the same way the registers would hold them. Then, the values from this stack can be popped into the hardware registers, and it will be as if the thread had always been running. The stack must have these values pushed on in a particular order, to be popped off into the correct registers.\\n",
